  "title": "Telepresence",
  "slug": "telepresence",
  "public": true,
  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:telepresence",
  "domain": "spatial-computing",
  "definition": "Telepresence is a suite of technologies and interaction paradigms that create a compelling perceptual sense of physical presence in a remote or virtual location, enabling natural communication, social interaction, and physical manipulation across geographic distance. Systems span high-definition video conferencing with matched room geometries and spatial audio, robotic telepresence platforms that provide mobile embodied presence, and fully immersive extended-reality environments that deliver volumetric representations and haptic feedback. The defining characteristic is the degree of presence \u2014 the subjective feeling of 'being there' \u2014 which depends on sensory fidelity, low latency, spatial coherence, and natural interaction affordances. Convergent advances in spatial computing, network infrastructure, and AI-driven media processing are progressively closing the gap between telepresent and co-located experience.",
